alta: AXI SRAM safety (2026-11-22). Applies on top of 0002-0004 (kit tree mesa-axi-sram) and 0002-0005 (mesa-strips).
- Shared outputs: backport of upstream Mesa's pipe_tensor::is_external_output. Teflon marks a partition's outputs while the
  driver compiles it; tensors that a CPU layer or the caller reads stay in RAM, so etna_ml_subgraph_read_outputs no longer
  aborts when an NPU layer and a CPU layer both read a tensor. Such a tensor also gets a detransposed copy that
  read_outputs returns: Mesa (upstream too) only detransposed outputs that nothing inside the subgraph reads, so the
  CPU got the NPU's channels-first layout (found on the NPU 2026-11-22, run SRAMFIX-S2-branch; also with the SRAM off).
- Not exclusive: the SRAM is one physical 1 MiB that every NPU program maps, so an SRAM tensor is only safe inside one
  hardware job. The SRAM is now refused with ETNA_MESA_DEBUG=npu_no_batching (one submit per operation) and npu_parallel
  (operations overlap, breaking the space reuse), and for partitions whose commands could pass libdrm's 0x4000-word
  command buffer (which would flush in the middle). Invoke flushes first when the batch wouldn't fit after what is queued,
  and warns once if a split is ever seen.
p_state.h changes: rebuild the whole teflon target.

